#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 415.5pt), 90pt, 86.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 84.14pt, "Abstract: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.54pt, 84.14pt, "Zigzag edges of graphene have long been predicted to exhibit magnetic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 99.74pt, "electronic state near the Fermi level, which can cause spin-related phenomena and offer ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 115.34pt, "unique potentials for graphene-based spintronics. However, the magnetic conduction ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 130.94pt, "channels along these edges have yet been reported experimentally. Here, we report the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 146.54pt, "observation on signatures of magnetism in zigzag graphene nanoribbons (zGNRs) ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 162.14pt, "embedded in hexagonal boron nitride (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(287.93pt, 162.14pt, "h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.95pt, 162.14pt, "-BN). The in-plane bonding with BN can ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 177.74pt, "stabilize the edges of zGNRs, and thus enable a direct probing of the intrinsic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.34pt, "magnetism. Firstly, the presence of magnetism of a zGNR was confirmed by scanning ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "NV center microscopy. And then, zGNR was fabricated into a transistor with a width ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "of ~9 nm wide and a channel length of sub-50 nm. By performing magneto-transport ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.14pt, "measurements, Fabry-Pérot interference patterns were observed in the transistor at 4 ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "Kelvin, which indicates a coherent transport through the channel. A large ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "magnetoresistance of ~175 Ω, corresponding to a ratio of ~1.3 %, was observed at the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "same temperature. More importantly, such magneto-transport signal is highly ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "anisotropic on the magnetic field direction, and its appearance extends well above room ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 318.17pt, "temperature. All these evidences corroborate the existence of robust magnetic ordering ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.77pt, "in the edge state of zGNR. The findings on zGNR embedded in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.7pt, 333.77pt, "h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(426.7pt, 333.77pt, "-BN provide an ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.37pt, "effective platform for the future exploration of graphene-based spintronic devices. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 396.17pt, "Zigzag graphene nanoribbons (zGNRs) are known as quasi one-dimensional strips of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.77pt, "graphene associated by parallel zigzag edges. These localized ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(418.54pt, 411.77pt, "zigzag edges are ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 427.39pt, "predicted to possess a unique magnetic state near the Fermi level")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(428.62pt, 422.83pt, "1 , 2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(441.22pt, 427.39pt, "  that can be ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 442.99pt, "promising for spintronic device applications. Recent progresses in GNRs synthesis ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 458.59pt, "enabled the fabrication of atomically precise GNRs, allowing the electrical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 474.19pt, "manipulation and detection of edge states. Symmetry protected topological phases,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(498.82pt, 469.63pt, "3-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 485.23pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(94.104pt, 489.79pt, " zero-mode metallicity")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(202.25pt, 485.23pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(206.33pt, 489.79pt, " and spin-polarized edge states")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(355.27pt, 485.23pt, "7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(359.35pt, 489.79pt, " are subsequently revealed via ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 505.39pt, "advanced scanning probe spectroscopy in GNRs")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(336.91pt, 505.39pt, ". However, a direct experimental ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 520.99pt, "probing of the magnetism by electrical methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(323.47pt, 520.99pt, "in zigzag edge structures")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(443.02pt, 520.99pt, " still remains ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 536.59pt, "elusive. Limited by surface diffusivity and kinetic factors on catalytic substrates, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 552.19pt, "GNRs")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.02pt, 547.63pt, "8,9 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.3pt, 552.19pt, "made from bottom-up assembly have length typically in the range of tens of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 567.79pt, "nanometers, which is too short to be technologically practical for reliable device ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 583.39pt, "fabrication. Moreover, the open edges of zGNRs")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(326.23pt, 578.83pt, "7,10-14")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(351.31pt, 583.39pt, " are of relatively high chemical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 599.02pt, "reactivity, and can thus cause instability or inhomogeneous doping in electronic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 614.62pt, "properties.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(146.18pt, 610.06pt, "16 -")
  #line-at(167.3pt, 610.06pt, "18")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(175.49pt, 614.62pt, "  Finally, the edge states in narrow zGNRs could become ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 630.22pt, "antiferromagnetically coupled so strongly that imposes difficulties detect sizable ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 645.82pt, "electrical signal under a moderate magnetic field.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(335.71pt, 641.26pt, "8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(339.79pt, 645.82pt, " All the above reasons hurdle the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 661.42pt, "direct transport measurement on the magnetism in GNR electronic device. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 692.62pt, "Successful fabrication of oriented zGNRs embedded in hexagonal boron nitride (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(474.7pt, 692.62pt, "h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.7pt, 692.62pt, "-BN) ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 708.22pt, "could potentially overcome the aforementioned difficulties and enable exploration of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 723.82pt, "spin transport in the ultimate limit of miniaturization.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(360.79pt, 719.26pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(368.95pt, 723.82pt, " The zigzag-oriented ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(478.9pt, 723.82pt, "h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(484.9pt, 723.82pt, "-BN ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 739.42pt, "trenches were produced by zinc nanoparticles cutting.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(362.95pt, 734.86pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(378.07pt, 739.42pt, "Subsequently, the zigzag-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 755.04pt, "oriented ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.1pt, 755.04pt, "h")
