  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(151.22pt, 84.14pt, " These zGNRs are now stabilized by in-plane graphene–BN bonding,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(487.3pt, 79.58pt, "22,23")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 99.74pt, "having a C-B interface at one edge and a C-N interface at the opposite edge. And thus ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 115.34pt, "narrow zGNRs were predicted to exhibit an insulating antiferromagnetic state")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(459.46pt, 110.78pt, "24-28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(478.54pt, 115.34pt, " with ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 130.94pt, "negligible contribution to electrical signal, similar to hydrogen terminated zGNRs")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.7pt, 126.38pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(484.78pt, 130.94pt, ". On ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 146.54pt, "another aspect, the asymmetric structure of zGNR/BN interface could in turn weaken ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 162.14pt, "the super-exchange interaction between the two inequivalent carbon edge states, so that ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 177.74pt, "now only a moderate magnetic field is required to manipulate the magnetic order of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.34pt, "zGNR.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.62pt, 188.78pt, "28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(135.98pt, 193.34pt, "More interestingly, it was further predicted that ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.47pt, 193.34pt, "the edges of zGNRs")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#222222"))
  #line-at(474.7pt, 193.34pt, " could ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "become a half")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.58pt, 208.94pt, "-metal once an in-plane homogeneous electric field is applied across the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "width direction.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.1pt, 219.98pt, "7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(170.18pt, 224.54pt, " Unfortunately, the transverse electric field required is experimentally ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.14pt, "too high (normally higher than one Volt per nm) to realize half-semimetallicity in ultra-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "narrow zGNRs.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(164.9pt, 251.21pt, "7,29")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(179.21pt, 255.77pt, " However, in a slightly wider zGNR, the super-exchange interaction ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "between edge states could become very weak. In addition, a built-in electric field is ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "naturally created by the difference of electrostatic potentials at the C-B and C-N ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "interfaces, which could promote the formation of half-semimetallicity in zGNRs’ edge ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 318.17pt, "states.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(119.66pt, 313.61pt, "30")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.82pt, 318.17pt, " As such, the zGNRs embedded in")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.85pt, 318.17pt, " h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(301.99pt, 318.17pt, "-BN provide a unique material platform to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.77pt, "detect the intrinsic edge state magnetism by transport measurement in a proper ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.37pt, "magnetic field, which could largely deepen the understanding of zGNR’s magnetic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 364.97pt, "properties.  ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 395.21pt, "A recently emerged scanning NV center microscope (SNVM) has become a powerful ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 409.01pt, "tool under ambient conditions to study spin textures in various magnetic materials.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(486.58pt, 404.45pt, "31-34")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 422.83pt, "By measuring the local magnetic field quantitatively via optical detection magnetic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 436.63pt, "resonance (ODMR)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.49pt, 432.07pt, "35,36")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(202.73pt, 436.63pt, ", the SNVM acquire nanoscale spatial resolution of the sample’s ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 452.35pt, "stray fields in a magnetic sensitivity of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(281.93pt, 452.35pt, "μT/√Hz")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(323.11pt, 452.35pt, ".")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(326.11pt, 447.79pt, " 37,38 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 482.71pt, "Firstly, we examine the presence of magnetism in zGNRs using SNVM, and then the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 498.31pt, "results are illustrated in figure 1. Figure 1b shows an AFM image of the region with ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 513.91pt, "zGNRs. Figure 1d shows the stray field in ISO-B mode for the same region shown in ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 529.51pt, "figure 1b. The contours of the magnetic domains extracted from PL mapping clearly ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 545.11pt, "shows the obvious contrast at the position of the zGNR. To exclude the contribution of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 560.71pt, "other origins to the PL signal, full-B mode imaging is adapted.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.43pt, 556.15pt, "33")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(395.59pt, 560.71pt, " As shown in figure 1e, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 576.31pt, "the full-B mode scanning exhibits a clearer and more distinct magnetic field distribution. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 591.94pt, "Crucially, its contours are consistent with those of the zGNR measured by AFM. The ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 607.54pt, "results of both scanning modes of SNVM confirm the magnetism of zGNR embedded ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 623.14pt, "in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(102.38pt, 623.14pt, "h")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.38pt, 623.14pt, "-BN. ")
]

